{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the first came out ruddy.</b> Midrash: when his father saw him he said, his blood has not yet been absorbed in him, and he did not want to circumcise him at eight days, as we say regarding the incident of the two women who came before Nathan the Babylonian, etc. When a year or two passed and Isaac saw that his appearance had not changed, he knew that this was his nature, and even so he did not circumcise him. He said: since I did not circumcise him at eight days like myself, I will wait until he is thirteen like my brother Ishmael, and then I will circumcise him. And when he was thirteen years old, he himself held back and did not want to be circumcised — and that is what is written: ״אם לא דם שנאת ודם ירדפך״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:01.091890296Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}